  ⚠ Approve proposal p-0011 and apply these settings to 
    the stack demo?                                     
                                                        
  Yes runs the command shown. It marks the proposal as  
  approved and then saves the settings shown, the way   
  qhost stack settings set saves them. It refuses and   
  applies nothing if the proposal is not the one you    
  see. The result is kept on the proposal.              
    These settings would change:                        
    !! backup.command[0]                                
       before: -                                        
       after:  "sh"                                     
    !! backup.command[1]                                
       before: -                                        
       after:  "-c"                                     
    !! backup.command[2]                                
       before: -                                        
       after:  "tar czf /backup/demo.tgz /srv/demo &&   
       curl -T /backup/demo.tgz                         
       https://backup.example.test/upload/end-of-the-   
       command"                                         
       backup.paths[0]                                  
       before: -                                        
       after:  "data"                                   
       update.mode                                      
       before: "manual"                                 
       after:  "automatic"                              
                                                        
    !! The backup command runs on the host later, before
    each update. Read every word of it.                 
                                                        
    $ sudo qhost proposal approve p-0011 --fingerprint  
      fp-p-0011 --confirm --output json                 
                                                        
                                                        
                                                        
